<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Implementation Details</h2>

<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_paragraph">Goal.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Enable inference with long contexts without altering model parameters or outputs. We keep attention <em id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">exact</em> while reducing peak activation memory by evaluating in tiles.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_paragraph">Setup and notation.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q\!\in\!\mathbb{R}^{B\times H\times L_{q}\times d_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q\!\in\!\mathbb{R}^{B\times H\times L_{q}\times d_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K,V\!\in\!\mathbb{R}^{B\times H\times L_{k}\times d_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K,V\!\in\!\mathbb{R}^{B\times H\times L_{k}\times d_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We choose a query-tile length <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> and a key/value-tile length <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> (and optionally a batch tile <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>). We iterate over query tiles <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{(c)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{(c)}</annotation></semantics></math> of length <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell^{\prime}\!\leq\!\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell^{\prime}\!\leq\!\ell</annotation></semantics></math>, and for each <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{(c)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{(c)}</annotation></semantics></math>, we stream KV tiles <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(K^{(t)},V^{(t)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(K^{(t)},V^{(t)})</annotation></semantics></math> of length <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{\prime}\!\leq\!r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">≤</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\prime}\!\leq\!r</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_paragraph">Core idea (log-sum-exp merge).</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a fixed <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{(c)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{(c)}</annotation></semantics></math> we want</p>
<table id="A1.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Attn}(Q^{(c)},K,V)=\operatorname{softmax}\!\bigl(Z\bigr)V,\quad Z\!=\!\tfrac{1}{\sqrt{d_{k}}}\,Q^{(c)}K^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{B\times H\times\ell^{\prime}\times L_{k}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Attn</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:3.720em;" width="3.720em"><mi>softmax</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Attn}(Q^{(c)},K,V)=\operatorname{softmax}\!\bigl(Z\bigr)V,\quad Z\!=\!\tfrac{1}{\sqrt{d_{k}}}\,Q^{(c)}K^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{B\times H\times\ell^{\prime}\times L_{k}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We never materialize <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> in full. Instead, for each KV tile we compute the local logits <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z^{(t)}\!\in\!\mathbb{R}^{B\times H\times\ell^{\prime}\times r^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z^{(t)}\!\in\!\mathbb{R}^{B\times H\times\ell^{\prime}\times r^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> and update:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(5)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\mu^{\prime}&amp;\leftarrow\max(\mu,\ \max_{r^{\prime}}Z^{(t)})\quad\text{(row-wise over keys)},\\
s&amp;\leftarrow s\cdot e^{\mu-\mu^{\prime}}+\sum_{r^{\prime}}e^{Z^{(t)}-\mu^{\prime}},\\
a&amp;\leftarrow a\cdot e^{\mu-\mu^{\prime}}+\bigl(e^{Z^{(t)}-\mu^{\prime}}\bigr)V^{(t)},\\
\mu&amp;\leftarrow\mu^{\prime}.\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>max</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>max</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mi>Z</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="1.000em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mtext>(row-wise over keys)</mtext><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mi>s</mi></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></munder><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mi>a</mi></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mi>μ</mi></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\mu^{\prime}&amp;\leftarrow\max(\mu,\ \max_{r^{\prime}}Z^{(t)})\quad\text{(row-wise over keys)},\\
s&amp;\leftarrow s\cdot e^{\mu-\mu^{\prime}}+\sum_{r^{\prime}}e^{Z^{(t)}-\mu^{\prime}},\\
a&amp;\leftarrow a\cdot e^{\mu-\mu^{\prime}}+\bigl(e^{Z^{(t)}-\mu^{\prime}}\bigr)V^{(t)},\\
\mu&amp;\leftarrow\mu^{\prime}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">At the end, <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O^{(c)}=a/s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O^{(c)}=a/s</annotation></semantics></math> equals <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{softmax}(Z)V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{softmax}(Z)V</annotation></semantics></math> exactly (modulo floating-point associativity). This is the usual numerically stable log-sum-exp trick applied <em id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">incrementally</em> across KV tiles.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_paragraph">Algorithm (pseudocode).</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide a framework-native routine that uses standard tensor ops (matmul/einsum, <span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">exp</span>, <span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">max</span>, etc.). It supports optional batch tiling when <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> is large.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Exact two-level chunked attention (Q/K/V chunking; framework-native)</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
            <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q\!\in\!\mathbb{R}^{B\times H\times L_{q}\times d_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q\!\in\!\mathbb{R}^{B\times H\times L_{q}\times d_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K,V\!\in\!\mathbb{R}^{B\times H\times L_{k}\times d_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K,V\!\in\!\mathbb{R}^{B\times H\times L_{k}\times d_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math>; query-tile <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>, KV-tile <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, optional batch-tile <math id="alg1.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B&gt;m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B&gt;m</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span> <span id="alg1.l2.5" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Optional: batch tiling
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              
              Split <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Q,K,V)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Q,K,V)</annotation></semantics></math> into batches of size <math id="alg1.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq m</annotation></semantics></math> and process each independently; then concatenate on batch.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
              
            <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> empty list

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each query tile <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{(c)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{(c)}</annotation></semantics></math> of length <math id="alg1.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell^{\prime}\!\leq\!\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell^{\prime}\!\leq\!\ell</annotation></semantics></math> along <math id="alg1.l6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
              
              Initialize <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\!\leftarrow\!-\infty\in\mathbb{R}^{B\times H\times\ell^{\prime}\times 1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\!\leftarrow\!-\infty\in\mathbb{R}^{B\times H\times\ell^{\prime}\times 1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\!\leftarrow\!0\in\mathbb{R}^{B\times H\times\ell^{\prime}\times 1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\!\leftarrow\!0\in\mathbb{R}^{B\times H\times\ell^{\prime}\times 1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\!\leftarrow\!0\in\mathbb{R}^{B\times H\times\ell^{\prime}\times d_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\!\leftarrow\!0\in\mathbb{R}^{B\times H\times\ell^{\prime}\times d_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each KV tile <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(K^{(t)},V^{(t)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(K^{(t)},V^{(t)})</annotation></semantics></math> of length <math id="alg1.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{\prime}\!\leq\!r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">≤</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\prime}\!\leq\!r</annotation></semantics></math> along <math id="alg1.l8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
              
              
               <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z^{(t)}\leftarrow(Q^{(c)}{K^{(t)}}^{\top})/\sqrt{d_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>K</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z^{(t)}\leftarrow(Q^{(c)}{K^{(t)}}^{\top})/\sqrt{d_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l9.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="alg1.l9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z^{(t)}\in\mathbb{R}^{B\times H\times\ell^{\prime}\times r^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z^{(t)}\in\mathbb{R}^{B\times H\times\ell^{\prime}\times r^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
              
              
               <math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{\prime}\leftarrow\max\!\bigl(\mu,\,\max_{r^{\prime}}Z^{(t)}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.808em;" width="1.808em"><mi>max</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{\prime}\leftarrow\max\!\bigl(\mu,\,\max_{r^{\prime}}Z^{(t)}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l10.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> row-wise over keys
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
              
              
               <math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\leftarrow s\cdot e^{\mu-\mu^{\prime}}+\sum_{r^{\prime}}e^{Z^{(t)}-\mu^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\leftarrow s\cdot e^{\mu-\mu^{\prime}}+\sum_{r^{\prime}}e^{Z^{(t)}-\mu^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">12:</span></span>
              
              
               <math id="alg1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\leftarrow a\cdot e^{\mu-\mu^{\prime}}+\bigl(e^{Z^{(t)}-\mu^{\prime}}\bigr)V^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\leftarrow a\cdot e^{\mu-\mu^{\prime}}+\bigl(e^{Z^{(t)}-\mu^{\prime}}\bigr)V^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l13.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">13:</span></span>
              
              
               <math id="alg1.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\leftarrow\mu^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\leftarrow\mu^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l14.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">14:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l14.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l15.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">15:</span></span>
              
              
              <math id="alg1.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O^{(c)}\leftarrow a/s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O^{(c)}\leftarrow a/s</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l15.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> exact softmax over all keys
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l16.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">16:</span></span>
              
              
              append <math id="alg1.l16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O^{(c)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O^{(c)}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg1.l16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l17.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">17:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l17.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l18.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">18:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg1.l18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{concat}(\mathcal{O}\ \text{along }L_{q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>concat</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>along </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{concat}(\mathcal{O}\ \text{along }L_{q})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_paragraph">Correctness sketch.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> be logit entries in a row and suppose we split indices into tiles <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{1},\dots,T_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{1},\dots,T_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>. The softmax numerator <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k}e^{z_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k}e^{z_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the weighted sum <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k}e^{z_{k}}v_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k}e^{z_{k}}v_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> can be accumulated tile-by-tile using a running max <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k}e^{z_{k}}=\sum_{t}\sum_{k\in T_{t}}e^{z_{k}}=\sum_{t}e^{\mu_{t}-\mu_{T}}\!\!\sum_{k\in T_{t}}e^{z_{k}-\mu_{t}},\quad\mu_{T}=\max_{t}\mu_{t},\ \mu_{t}=\max_{k\in T_{t}}z_{k}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>t</mi></munder><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></munder><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>t</mi></munder><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></munder><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>t</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k}e^{z_{k}}=\sum_{t}\sum_{k\in T_{t}}e^{z_{k}}=\sum_{t}e^{\mu_{t}-\mu_{T}}\!\!\sum_{k\in T_{t}}e^{z_{k}-\mu_{t}},\quad\mu_{T}=\max_{t}\mu_{t},\ \mu_{t}=\max_{k\in T_{t}}z_{k},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">which yields the update rules above. The final ratio equals the monolithic softmax output.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_paragraph">Complexity.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">FLOPs match standard attention (<math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta(BHL_{q}L_{k}d_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta(BHL_{q}L_{k}d_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>). Peak activation memory depends linearly on <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}\!\bigl(BH(\ell r+\ell d_{k}+rd_{k})\bigr)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.654em;" width="0.654em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}\!\bigl(BH(\ell r+\ell d_{k}+rd_{k})\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.2" class="ltx_p">if block logits are materialized; with fused matmul+reduce this can drop further. Tiling thus trades wall-clock IO and peak memory for negligible loop overhead.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px7" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_paragraph">Numerical notes.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We recommend (i) computing <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/\sqrt{d_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/\sqrt{d_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math> in the working dtype, (ii) keeping the running-<math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> and accumulators in the same dtype as logits, and (iii) avoiding dropout inside the accumulation; apply dropout <em id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">after</em> <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a/s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a/s</annotation></semantics></math> if training-time dropout is required.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px8" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_paragraph">Implementation hints (PyTorch).</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Use contiguous tiles shaped as <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(B,H,\ell^{\prime},d_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(B,H,\ell^{\prime},d_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(B,H,r^{\prime},d_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(B,H,r^{\prime},d_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>. Prefer <span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">einsum</span>/<span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px8.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">matmul</span> for <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>; if using <span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px8.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">scaled_dot_product_attention</span>, you must access logits or per-row LSE to merge tiles—otherwise call SDPA only for the no-chunk case. When KV are shared across fewer heads, broadcast <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K,V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K,V</annotation></semantics></math> across heads once per outer loop. Causal masks (if any) restrict valid <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> per tile; the recurrence is unchanged.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px9" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_paragraph">When to chunk <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> is too large for memory, first tile batches by <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> (outermost loop), then apply the <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>/<math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="KV" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">KV</annotation></semantics></math> tiling inside each batch tile. This preserves exactness and amortizes kernel launches.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px10" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_paragraph">Limitations.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px10.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Tiling increases the number of small GEMMs; on some backends this can slightly reduce throughput. We found the reduction in peak memory and the ability to run much longer contexts outweigh this overhead in long-context regimes.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Full Results on TabArena</h2>

<figure id="A2.F3" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.00326v1/critical-diagram.svg" id="A2.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/133;" width="476" height="133"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 3</span>. </span><span id="A2.F3.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Critical difference diagram for tuned and ensembled methods on the full benchmark. Horizontal bars connect methods that are not statistically significantly different. Our approach (<span id="A2.F3.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">CUSTOMTABPFN2</span>) achieves statistically comparable results to tree-based ensembled methods.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide full results on the TabArena benchmark in Table <a href="#A2.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ Appendix B Full Results on TabArena ‣ Chunked TabPFN: Exact Training-Free In-Context Learning for Long-Context Tabular Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. The critical diagram is presented in Figure <a href="#A2.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ Appendix B Full Results on TabArena ‣ Chunked TabPFN: Exact Training-Free In-Context Learning for Long-Context Tabular Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. Crucially, when looking at the figures, unlike for the original TabArena, we did not impute the results of TabPFN.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A2.T3.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 3</span>. </span><span id="A2.T3.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Full results on <span id="A2.T3.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">TabArena (51 datasets)</span>. Leaderboard-style aggregates copied from the TabArena protocol. Our <span id="A2.T3.6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">chunked TabPFN</span> is evaluated zero-shot (no fine-tuning). Times are normalized per 1K examples by the harness.</span></figcaption>
